#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""BONANZA's course compiler, waves 1 - 4 (SPEC.md 130.10.3 - 130.10.7, 130.11, 130.12, 130.14).

    python3 tools/bbcourse.py -o DIR COURSE.bbc ...        # what `make` runs: every
                                                          # course, in BZ_COURSES's order,
                                                          # and every course's demo (K 1 ..)
    python3 tools/bbcourse.py --selfcheck [COURSE.bbc ...] # SPEC.md 130.11.17.1, 130.14.18 item 9
    python3 tools/bbcourse.py COURSE.bbc --png DIR         # previews (Pillow, behind a try)
    python3 tools/bbcourse.py demo IN.BZR [-o OUT.bzd]     # a saved log as a .bzd (130.14.7.4)
    python3 tools/bbcourse.py author COURSE.bbc [-o OUT]   # an AUTHOR script's .bzd (130.14.18 item 7)
    python3 tools/bbcourse.py --tune HOP=r,s,g BOOST=b ... # a retune checked first, nothing written
                                                          # (SPEC.md 130.16.13)

Wave 8R (SPEC.md 130.22): THE PATHWAY's `pages`, `pad N`, `icon`, `route`
(gate, secret, path), `lives` and `rail`; PK_SIGN records (pads, icons,
gates, reveals); the tables at PTHOFF (path_tables, read_path_tables); the
key map; the graph and course proofs; `Follow`, the follower's host model;
the clock-at-every-finish rule (finish_clock_rule) and the demos' identity
re-stamp it allows (clock_restamp).

Wave 6b (SPEC.md 130.17): GRIP 6, 3, 1 and ice's rounded brake; the boost
ARMED by a second Space edge in flight (bz_btok 2) and the LATE GRACE
(BGRACE, bgr/bgd in state6()); PHYS_REV 7; the ladders swept at
arm_positions(); item 7's offset map, the grace's exactness, the ledge and
accidental cases, who-hits-it against wave 6's trigger, CD5's table.

Gate 1's round 3 (SPEC.md 130.17.16): BGRACE 4; Space HELD at a first
contact arms the boost onto a floor no higher than the take-off (zoff); a
FALL takes the token; PHYS_REV 8; item 7's held, fall and stop-bouncing
checks (fall_boosts(), fall_spent()) and their controls.

Gate 1's round 3b (SPEC.md 130.17.17): every launch takes the token (bsp,
the boost spent until the ball is on the ground, for a launch out of the
air); the boost ADDED to the bounce (badd(), BZ_MATTAB +14), rule 5 gone; the
reach's added boost; PHYS_REV 9; _launch_checks().

Wave 6 (SPEC.md 130.16): the material table with BOOST (BZ_MATTAB +12) and
its import-time bound; the fractional drag and the boost's token in
Physics (state6()); the reach's BOOST launch from every firm level floor;
axis_feel(), the independent axis model item 7 asserts Physics against;
the STEP and GAP LADDERS; PHYS_REV and PHYSV_SHIPPED; the `palette`
statement and BZ_CRS_PALS; AUTHOR's hop, boost and grip verbs; a shipped
.bzd under other physics REFUSED; --tune.

Wave 4 (SPEC.md 130.14.4, 130.14.18): `par`, `checkpoint`, `pad`, `cup`,
`spring` and `way ... branch`; prop kinds 5 - 8 (a flag a two-pose lane, the
rest static marks), BZG1 +28 / +29, BZ_CRS_PARS, BZ_CRS_IDS and BZ_PHYSV;
the model's RETURN, flags, pads, cup, springs and tilt caps; NO TRAP (wave
4's NOTHING UNDER THE HUD went with the HUD in wave 5a, SPEC.md 130.15.3);
the shipped demos BZD<K>.BIN from text or the route.

A course is TEXT (`apps/bonanza/courses/*.bbc`, SPEC.md 130.10.3, with
wave 2's `surface` and `ball`, 130.11.6.1).  ONE run compiles the whole list:
course K (its place on the command line) becomes ONE part, `BZ<K>.BIN`, a
`BZC1` part carrying the picture (a flat map of absolute block offsets and
the deduplicated 8 x 8 CGA blocks - the guest translates them in place on the
Hercules through htab(), SPEC.md 130.11.3), the occluder records (MERGED
exactly where no reachable position tells two apart, 130.11.4.1) and masks,
and the `BZG1` physics grid (SPEC.md 130.10.5; surfaces and OCCG,
130.11.2); and the same run writes `bzcourse.inc` WHOLE - `BZ_NCRS`, each
course's name, title and ball, the materials and surfaces tables, and the
`OS88_PART` rows of every course part (SPEC.md 130.11.3.1).  A stamp,
`.bz-crs`, holding a hash of this tool, of tools/bonanza_assets.py (whose
palette and Hercules encoders it imports) and of every course file, is
written FIRST.

Deterministic (the same inputs give the same bytes), standard library only,
integer geometry throughout (Fraction where a ramp's height at a pixel is a
ratio).  The renderer MOVED here from tools/bonanza_assets.py (SPEC.md
130.10.4); the palette, `cga_bytes`, `herc_pair`, `herc_bytes` and `htab`
are IMPORTED from there, so a course and the ball cannot disagree about a
mid-level pixel.

The run checks what it wrote, at BUILD time (packages are trusted, so the
guest does not): `read_part` re-reads every part as the guest would and
refuses a bad magic, offset, count, map word, OCCIDX, ROWTAB row, mask
offset, route, kind, surface or flag, naming the course and the field.

Wave 3 (SPEC.md 130.12): `tube` and `prop` statements; the prop table after
the grid (BZC1 +28 / +30: records, pose maps, tube segments, the platform's
sprite), the grid's OBS bit, each lane's poses rendered into the one block
pool, the course's IDENTITY at BZG1 +18, and every refusal and bound of
130.12.3.3 and 130.12.4.6 - the exits checked by the model, the lanes'
occluder verdicts checked over every pose.

`Physics` is SPEC.md 130.11.8's step (wave 1's, 130.10.7.3, as wave 2
changes it, with wave 3's obstacles, 130.12.6.5), integer-exact: the
guest's bzphys.inc is written to do exactly what it does, and the
bonanzaphys row compares the two at every frame (state3() is wave 3's
part of the state).
`MATERIALS` is the one place the balls' constants are written.

Host reference for the rows (import this module):
    compile_course(path_or_text)    -> Course: .pic (the CGA picture, a list of
                                       bytearray rows), .cga (THE part), .herc
                                       (the part as the guest translates it on
                                       the Hercules), .sbuf/.tbuf (the per-pixel
                                       cell row and top), .records (merged),
                                       .raw (unmerged), .by_block, .cells,
                                       .reach, .x0, .y0, .route, .ball ...
    read_part(bytes)                -> the parsed part (and its build checks)
    Grid(part).cell(wx, wy)         -> (z0, sx, sy, kind, flags, surface), OPEN
                                       outside
    Physics(course, play=False, mat=None)
                                    -> the model: .step(key byte), .step_auto(),
                                       .poke(wx, wy, gvx, gvy), .run_log(log),
                                       the guest's state as .gx .gy .gz .gvx
                                       .gvy .gvz .air .nstep ... and wave 2's
                                       .lvl .hopw .kprev .mst .mct .sqf .lvz
                                       .gh .ghv (state2()), the screen state
                                       .bx .by .vx .vy, and .events
    Glide(physics, herc, brows, cols), glide_run(course, herc, rate, phase)
                                    -> GLIDE, bz_lattice's model (130.11.11.1;
                                       LATTICE since wave 6b, 130.17.6; _w6
                                       wave 6's policy, scripted=True
                                       bz_camscr's camera)
    camcheck(courses, demos, res)   -> --camcheck, item 8's camera checks
                                       (130.17.9); CamRun, cam_demo, cam_auto
                                       its harness
    encode_log(keys, course, mat), decode_log(log)   BZR1 (130.11.12.1)
    ledge_gaps(), gap_table_text()  -> 130.11.5.3's table, from Physics
    htab(), herc_translate_course(part)              130.11.3
    laid_at(course, px, py, sb, zb, air, card=False)
                                    the records the guest's pass lays (card:
                                       the pixels the CARD lays, less the
                                       ghost checker's, 130.15.10.3)
    composite(course, px, py, sb, zb, air, via, ghost=False)
                                    the ball over the picture with the
                                       occluders laid back through the RECORDS
                                       (the ring's oracle, SPEC.md 130.10.11.3;
                                       ghost: the card's model, the dither)
    ghost(x, y), CHK, dither(mask)  the ghost dither (SPEC.md 130.15.10.1)
    card_composite(course, ...)     the card's composite read out of the RAM
                                       part's dithered masks (item 11)
    Follow(points, reverse=False)   SPEC.md 130.22.4.2: the follower, .step()
                                       -> (bz_gx, bz_gy, bz_gz) 24.8, .s .v
                                       .arrived; a course's .pth and
                                       .part["path"] (the tables read back)
    visibility(course, k, demo)     the visibility audit, REPORT mode
                                       (SPEC.md 130.15.10.4)
"""
